Let's analyze the constraints. $N, M \le 2025$. This suggests an algorithm with complexity around $O(N^2)$ or $O(N^3)$ might be acceptable, but $O(N^2)$ is safer.

The condition $x_i \le x_{A_i}$ defines a set of dependencies. Specifically, if we view the indices $1, \dots, N$ as nodes in a directed graph where there is an edge from $i$ to $A_i$, then the condition says that the value at node $i$ must be less than or equal to the value at node $A_i$.
