For a query $(L, R)$, we consider the subarray $A[L \dots R]$.
We want to form pairs $(a, b)$ such that $a \le b/2$. Each pair forms one kagamimochi. We want to maximize the number of pairs.
Let the chosen subset of mochi be $S$. We partition $S$ into $K$ pairs $(x_1, y_1), \dots, (x_K, y_K)$ such that $x_j \le y_j/2$ for all $j$. The goal is to maximize $K$.

